WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.932
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:08.595
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:15.193
Unit thirteen: Simple Science Experiments. In this unit, you will describe an experiment in order.

4
00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:17.184
Experiment.

5
00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.464
Experiment means a test to discover something.

6
00:00:20.764 --> 00:00:22.834
We did an experiment with ice.

7
00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:26.488
Your turn. Say: Experiment.

8
00:00:29.188 --> 00:00:30.247
Experiment.

9
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.263
Science.

10
00:00:32.963 --> 00:00:35.264
Science means the study of the natural world.

11
00:00:35.564 --> 00:00:37.564
Science is my favourite subject.

12
00:00:38.264 --> 00:00:40.486
Your turn. Say: Science.

13
00:00:43.186 --> 00:00:44.211
Science.

14
00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:46.450
Hypothesis.

15
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.916
Hypothesis means a guess you test in an experiment.

16
00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.900
My hypothesis was that salt melts ice.

17
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.404
Your turn. Say: Hypothesis.

18
00:00:59.104 --> 00:01:00.267
Hypothesis.

19
00:01:01.283 --> 00:01:02.157
Result.

20
00:01:02.857 --> 00:01:05.623
Result means what happens at the end of an experiment.

21
00:01:05.923 --> 00:01:07.411
The result surprised us.

22
00:01:08.111 --> 00:01:10.369
Your turn. Say: Result.

23
00:01:13.069 --> 00:01:14.000
Result.

24
00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:15.902
Mix.

25
00:01:16.602 --> 00:01:18.601
Mix means to put things together.

26
00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.610
Mix the water and the salt.

27
00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.870
Your turn. Say: Mix.

28
00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:27.420
Mix.

29
00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:29.290
Measure.

30
00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:33.069
Measure means to find the size or amount of something.

31
00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:35.682
Measure fifty millilitres of water.

32
00:01:36.382 --> 00:01:38.489
Your turn. Say: Measure.

33
00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:41.981
Measure.

34
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:43.915
Observe.

35
00:01:44.615 --> 00:01:46.614
Observe means to watch carefully.

36
00:01:46.914 --> 00:01:48.786
Observe what happens to the egg.

37
00:01:49.486 --> 00:01:52.289
Your turn. Say: Observe.

38
00:01:54.989 --> 00:01:55.898
Observe.

39
00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:57.908
Safety.

40
00:01:58.608 --> 00:02:00.816
Safety means being safe from danger.

41
00:02:01.116 --> 00:02:02.744
Wear goggles for safety.

42
00:02:03.444 --> 00:02:06.155
Your turn. Say: Safety.

43
00:02:08.855 --> 00:02:09.705
Safety.

44
00:02:10.717 --> 00:02:12.797
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:13.097 --> 00:02:16.095
Sreypich, what experiment did you do in science?

46
00:02:17.383 --> 00:02:19.859
We tested if an egg floats in salt water.

47
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.569
What did you do first?

48
00:02:23.883 --> 00:02:28.010
First, we made a hypothesis. Then, we mixed water and salt.

49
00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:30.504
And finally?

50
00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:34.655
Finally, we observed. The egg floated!

51
00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:39.459
Grammar focus: Sequencing (first, then, finally).

52
00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:43.598
First, we measured. Then, we mixed. Finally, we observed.

53
00:02:43.898 --> 00:02:48.405
When you describe a past experiment, use sequencing words with the past simple.

54
00:02:49.417 --> 00:02:51.976
Now read and listen. The Floating Egg.

55
00:02:52.276 --> 00:02:55.379
In science class, we did an experiment with an egg.

56
00:02:56.683 --> 00:03:00.482
First, we made a hypothesis: the egg will float in salt water.

57
00:03:01.783 --> 00:03:04.468
Then, we measured the water and mixed in some salt.

58
00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:08.677
Finally, we put the egg in and observed the result.

59
00:03:09.983 --> 00:03:13.541
The egg floated! We always follow safety rules in the lab.

60
00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:17.270
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.151
blank, we made a hypothesis. (step 1)

62
00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:24.385
A, First. B, Finally. C, Then.

63
00:03:28.383 --> 00:03:29.953
The answer is A: First.

64
00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.809
A guess you test in an experiment is a blank.

65
00:03:34.109 --> 00:03:38.169
A, hypothesis. B, result. C, safety.

66
00:03:42.183 --> 00:03:44.845
The answer is A: hypothesis.

67
00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.129
To watch carefully is to blank.

68
00:03:48.429 --> 00:03:51.513
A, observe. B, measure. C, mix.

69
00:03:55.517 --> 00:03:57.214
The answer is A: observe.

70
00:03:58.717 --> 00:04:02.263
Now it's your turn to speak. What experiment would you like to try?

71
00:04:07.563 --> 00:04:15.399
I would like to make a volcano. First, I'd make it from clay. Then, I'd mix vinegar and baking soda. Finally, I'd watch it erupt!

72
00:04:15.699 --> 00:04:18.105
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:19.117 --> 00:04:23.998
Great work today! You learned eight new words and sequencing (first, then, finally).

74
00:04:24.298 --> 00:04:28.030
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

75
00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.785
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:31.085 --> 00:04:34.202
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

